{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on 0493e063 (S4 management). I read both plans, 5214c714 and\nb6ab26c7. Both choices are approved, with one change of words.\n\n1. The actor-only read. Approved as plan b6ab26c7 states it. The same\n   `hostedRoleStanding` RPC takes a second exact request,\n   {membership, actor}, and answers {status, of, head, actor} or\n   unavailable. The five-field Agent request and its reply keep their\n   bytes. One authority path, one decoder and one owner stay easier to\n   review than a second RPC.\n\n   Conditions:\n   - The exact key set selects the shape. A mixed, missing or extra\n     field answers unavailable.\n   - The actor reply holds the facts of that one key only. It lists no\n     other member and no roster text.\n   - S4's head states the second request shape where\n     docs/security/entry-points.md describes the RPC.\n\n2. The stop after a committed cleanup. Approved: the existing 503 with\n   `error: \"temporarily_unavailable\"`. A 202 would promise that the\n   server finishes alone, and it does not. The committed grant ends,\n   the erased seed, bearer and session, and the first revoke envelope\n   all stay. No rollback, no new mint, no new signature.\n\n   Change the `next` text. \"Reconcile the original\" names no action\n   that a client can take. Use:\n\n   \"The cleanup may already be in effect. Send the same operation\n   again. Do not start a new operation.\"\n\n   If the client must do a named step before it sends again, name that\n   step in the text and tell me. The body holds `error` and `next`\n   only. Before any commit, a valid denial stays 403 and unavailable\n   facts or clock stay 503 with no effect, as you propose.\n\nIdentifiers (b) keeps the slot. `MCP_ENABLED` stays off on every Worker\nuntil S4 lands.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}